  "body": "## What changed\n- The Stock page Source picker writes the part that it shows into the stock draft. It does this each frame when the two differ.\n- Apply now submits the shown part. The user does not have to change Source first.\n- A new decision file records the choice: `docs/decisions/3261-stock-source-default.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- `source_fields` wrote the name into the draft only when the selection index changed.\n- With an empty draft, the picker shows the last eligible model. The draft stays empty.\n- With one model, the index cannot change. Apply submitted an empty source, and stock creation failed.\n\n## Tests\n- New file `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/stock_source_default.rs`:\n  - `from_model_apply_takes_the_only_part_shown`: a blank project with exactly one imported part and no prior stock. The part name is visible before Apply. The stock source is the part name.\n  - `from_model_apply_takes_the_part_shown_of_several`: a blank project with two imported parts and no prior stock. The shown part name is visible before Apply. The applied source is the shown part.\n- Red before the fix: yes. The one-part test got `None` for the stock source. The two-part test found an empty draft.\n- Mutation checks: the seeded harness makes both model-count checks red. The blank harness restores green. The old `stock_page.rs` makes both application pins red. Restoring the fix makes them green.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): green, 10 steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Stock page screenshots\n\nBoth captures use a blank project with one imported part named `box`.\nThe harness renders the real Stock page and the 3D viewport.\nThe steps select From model and click Apply without changing Source.\n\nBefore: the original Source logic leaves the source empty. Apply refuses the stock.\n\n![Stock page before the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a0c37b16c84a536ffc200219c2d487f24fca7e8a/3268/stock-from-model-before.png)\n\nAfter: Apply creates stock from `box`.\n\n![Stock page after the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/a0c37b16c84a536ffc200219c2d487f24fca7e8a/3268/stock-from-model-after.png)\n\nThe images exist only on the fork's `pr-screenshots` branch.\nNo screenshots or capture helpers are in the PR branch.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The desktop app on macOS was not started. The pins drive the real page through the test harness.\n- Save and reopen of the project was not tested. The issue reports that this works when the command receives a name.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #3057 touches `crates/ui/src/egui_app/stock_page.rs`, in `stock_page` only. This PR changes `source_fields`. It is the same file and a different function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Stock \"From model\" now applies the part that Source shows, also when only one part is in the project.\n\nFixes #3261\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
